export const retainedVertexPrompt = "Build a complete, premium, responsive five-page website for Vertex AI Studio, an international technology agency specializing in artificial intelligence, custom software, automation and data engineering.\n\nDesign:\nUse dark navy (#0B1120), electric blue (#3B82F6) and subtle violet accents. Include elegant typography, generous spacing, refined gradients, polished cards and subtle CSS animations. Keep the visual identity consistent across every page.\n\nCreate exactly these five pages:\n\nPage 1 — Home (/)\n- Hero headline: “Engineering Ideas Into Intelligent Products”\n- Supporting description about developing AI-powered products and modern software\n- “Explore Our Work” linking to /work\n- “Start a Project” linking to /contact\n- CSS technology showcase\n- Four service cards linking to /services\n- Featured projects linking to /work\n- Four-step process timeline\n- Three fictional client testimonials\n- FAQ accordion with five meaningful answers\n- Final contact CTA\n\nPage 2 — Services (/services)\n- Four functional service tabs:\n  AI Development, AI Agents & Automation, Web Applications and Data Engineering\n- Switching tabs displays the corresponding service description, benefits, technology stack and example use cases\n- Clear selected-tab state\n- Contact CTA linking to /contact\n\nPage 3 — Our Work (/work)\n- At least eight realistic fictional projects\n- Categories: AI, Web, Automation and Data\n- Working category filters with an All option\n- Search that filters projects by name or description\n- Search and category filters work together\n- Useful empty-results feedback\n- Project cards showing descriptions, technology stacks and outcomes\n- Selecting a project opens an accessible detail dialog with meaningful project-specific content\n- Every visible Close control closes the dialog\n- Opening another project shows that project's details\n\nPage 4 — About (/about)\n- Company story, mission and values\n- Four fictional team profiles\n- Company milestones\n- Technology expertise\n- Contact CTA linking to /contact\n\nPage 5 — Contact (/contact)\n- Project inquiry form with:\n  name, email, company, service type, budget range and message\n- Name, email, service type and message are required\n- Validate email format\n- Preserve entered values when validation fails\n- After valid submission, show an on-page inquiry summary and clearly state:\n  “Demo only — your inquiry has not been sent or stored.”\n- Fictional business contact information\n\nShared functionality:\n- Working navigation between all five pages\n- Active navigation states\n- Mobile menu that opens, closes and closes after navigation\n- Every internal link points to a real page or section\n- Responsive layouts without horizontal overflow\n- Accessible labels, readable contrast and keyboard-operable controls\n- Useful dialog sizing on mobile\n- No browser runtime errors\n\nUse reusable React components, React state and local sample data. Implement genuine frontend behavior for every visible interactive control. Do not use empty handlers, JavaScript alert placeholders or decorative controls presented as functional.\n\nDo not add authentication, real payments, external APIs or backend submissions. Deliver the complete website rather than a single-page mockup.";
